  "body": {
    "id": "thm:crossfit-attainment",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "Suppose \\(P\\) is a fixed conditional-mean interior law induced by the global OVS model, \\(X\\) has fixed finite support with every support mass bounded below, and every first stage in Definition \\(\\ref{def:crossfit-estimator}\\) is its corresponding training-cell average.  Under independent fixed-\\(T\\) sampling, global retained-cell overlap, the global conditional fourth-moment envelope, fixed-fold cross-fitting, the threshold condition, and \\(V_{\\mathrm{OVS}}>0\\), take \\(\\tau_n=n^{-a}\\) for \\(0<a<1/4\\).  Then\n\\[\n\\sqrt n\\{\\widehat\\tau_{\\mathrm{eff}}-\\tau_\\omega(P)\\}\n=\\frac1{\\sqrt n}\\sum_{i=1}^n\\phi_{\\mathrm{OVS},P}(O_i)+o_P(1)\n\\ \\Rightarrow\\ N(0,V_{\\mathrm{OVS}}),\n\\tag{41}\n\\]\n\\[\n\\widehat V_{\\mathrm{eff}}\\longrightarrow_P V_{\\mathrm{OVS}},\n\\qquad\nP\\{\\tau_\\omega(P)\\in\\mathrm{CI}_{1-\\alpha}\\}\\longrightarrow1-\\alpha.\n\\tag{42}\n\\]\nThus the OVS-complete-normal estimator attains the pointwise semiparametric efficiency bound of the published class.  The local complete-normal correction remains regular on the published subclass but need not attain its smaller bound.  No continuous-covariate, rank-uniform, or equality-boundary inference claim is made.",
