    "justification": "The exhaustive augmented OVS signal converts the published population projection into an attainable pointwise estimator on fixed finite support.",
    "gap": "The proof deliberately excludes continuous covariates and rank-uniform sequences.",
    "consumer": "A CRAN \\(\\texttt{triplediff}\\) optional backend can implement this verified discrete-covariate branch and its Wald interval.",
    "proof_tex": "Let \\(\\eta=(p,m)\\),\n\\[\n\\alpha_{\\mathrm{OVS},P}(X)=K_{\\mathrm{OVS},P}(X)^\\dagger r_{\\mathrm{OVS},P}(X),\n\\qquad\n\\mu_P(O)=\\sum_{k\\in\\mathcal K}\\omega_kR_{k,c_0(k),P}(O).\n\\]\nConditional on a training complement, validation observations are independent of foldwise estimates.  For \\(k=(g,t)\\), write \\(M_{a,s,k}=\\sum_{u=g}^tm_{a,s,u}\\), and let \\(B_{k,c}\\) be the bracketed numerator in Definition \\(\\ref{def:pairwise-score}\\).  Adding and subtracting true regressions gives the exact conditional identity\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\nE_P[\\widehat B_{k,c}-B_{k,c}\\mid X]\n={}&\\left(\\frac{\\widehat p_{g,1}p_{g,0}}{\\widehat p_{g,0}}-p_{g,1}\\right)\n(\\widehat M_{g,0,k}-M_{g,0,k})\\\\\n&+\\left(\\frac{\\widehat p_{g,1}p_{c,1}}{\\widehat p_{c,1}}-p_{g,1}\\right)\n(\\widehat M_{c,1,k}-M_{c,1,k})\\\\\n&+\\left(p_{g,1}-\\frac{\\widehat p_{g,1}p_{c,0}}{\\widehat p_{c,0}}\\right)\n(\\widehat M_{c,0,k}-M_{c,0,k}).\n\\end{aligned}\n\\tag{A1}\n\\]\nOverlap makes every coefficient Lipschitz in \\(\\widehat p-p\\).  Fixed dimension and H\\\"older's inequality imply\n\\[\n|P\\{\\mu(O;\\widehat\\eta)-\\mu(O;\\eta)\\}|\n\\le C\\|\\widehat p-p\\|_{P_X,4}\\|\\widehat m-m\\|_{P_X,4}\n=O_P(n^{-1}).\n\\tag{A2}\n\\]\n\nLemma \\(\\ref{lem:ovs-orthogonal-normal-signal}\\) and the OVS equalities give\n\\[\n\\|E_P[\\widehat S^{\\mathrm{OVS},-\\ell}\\mid X,\\mathcal D_{-\\ell}]\\|_{P_X,2}\n=O_P(n^{-1}),\n\\qquad S^{\\mathrm{OVS}}(O;\\eta)=Z_P^{\\mathrm{OVS}}(O).\n\\tag{A3}\n\\]\nProposition \\(\\ref{prop:ovs-normal-finite-support-rates}\\) gives\n\\[\n\\max_\\ell\\|\\widehat\\alpha_{\\mathrm{OVS}}^{-\\ell}-\\alpha_{\\mathrm{OVS},P}\\|_{P_X,4}\n=O_P(n^{-1/2+a})=o_P(1).\n\\tag{A4}\n\\]\nThe conditional fourth-moment envelope, nuisance consistency, and (A4) yield\n\\[\n\\|\\widehat\\alpha_{\\mathrm{OVS}}^{-\\ell}(X)'\\widehat S^{\\mathrm{OVS},-\\ell}\n-\\alpha_{\\mathrm{OVS},P}(X)'Z_P^{\\mathrm{OVS}}\\|_{P,2}=o_P(1).\n\\tag{A5}\n\\]\nEquations (A3)--(A4) also make the conditional mean of (A5) of order \\(O_P(n^{-1})\\).  Conditional Chebyshev inequality fold by fold, followed by summation over the fixed number of folds, gives\n\\[\n\\widehat\\tau_{\\mathrm{eff}}-\\tau_\\omega(P)\n=(\\mathbb P_n-P)\\{\\mu_P-\\alpha_{\\mathrm{OVS},P}(X)'Z_P^{\\mathrm{OVS}}\\}\n+o_P(n^{-1/2}),\n\\tag{A6}\n\\]\napart from the empirical target-share contribution.\n\nOverlap gives \\(\\pi_{g,1}>0\\), and Taylor expansion of the global empirical share gives\n\\[\n\\widehat\\pi_{g,1}^{-1}-\\pi_{g,1}^{-1}\n=-\\pi_{g,1}^{-2}(\\widehat\\pi_{g,1}-\\pi_{g,1})+O_P(n^{-1}).\n\\tag{A7}\n\\]\nThe expectation of the bracketed numerator for block \\(k=(g,t)\\) is \\(\\pi_{g,1}\\theta_k(P)\\).  Thus (A7) contributes\n\\[\n-\\sum_{k=(g,t)\\in\\mathcal K}\\omega_k\\frac{\\theta_k(P)}{\\pi_{g,1}}\n(\\mathbb P_n-P)\\mathbf 1\\{G=g,S=1\\}+o_P(n^{-1/2}).\n\\tag{A8}\n\\]\nBy Definition \\(\\ref{def:pairwise-score}\\), combining (A6) and (A8) replaces \\(\\mu_P-E_P\\mu_P\\) by \\(\\psi_P^0\\).  Hence\n\\[\n\\sqrt n\\{\\widehat\\tau_{\\mathrm{eff}}-\\tau_\\omega(P)\\}\n=\\frac1{\\sqrt n}\\sum_{i=1}^n\n\\{\\psi_P^0(O_i)-\\alpha_{\\mathrm{OVS},P}(X_i)'Z_P^{\\mathrm{OVS}}(O_i)\\}+o_P(1)\n=\\frac1{\\sqrt n}\\sum_{i=1}^n\\phi_{\\mathrm{OVS},P}(O_i)+o_P(1).\n\\tag{A9}\n\\]\nThe summands are iid, mean zero, square integrable by overlap and the fourth-moment envelope, and have variance \\(V_{\\mathrm{OVS}}>0\\).  Lemma \\(\\ref{lem:iid-central-limit}\\) proves the Gaussian limit.  Equations (A4)--(A5), root-\\(n\\) consistency of the finite cell ratios and shares, and conditional Chebyshev imply\n\\[\n\\mathbb P_n(\\widehat\\phi-\\phi_{\\mathrm{OVS},P})^2=o_P(1).\n\\]\nExpanding the centered empirical second moment proves \\(\\widehat V_{\\mathrm{eff}}\\to_PV_{\\mathrm{OVS}}\\).  Positivity of the limit places the studentizing factor within \\((1-\\epsilon,1+\\epsilon)\\) with probability tending to one for every \\(\\epsilon>0\\); sandwiching at Gaussian continuity points proves the stated Wald coverage.  Theorem \\(\\ref{thm:complete-normal-canonical-gradient}\\) identifies this variance as the published-class efficiency bound.",
